{"duration_api_ms":91307,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"fab23369-38b6-42e6-96e3-28ec584874cb","total_cost_usd":0.434235,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":82440,"cache_read_input_tokens":95285,"output_tokens":8541,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3503},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":82440,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2464,"cache_read_input_tokens":85745,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6235,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6235},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":8541,"cacheReadInputTokens":95285,"cacheCreationInputTokens":82440,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.434235,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3503,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"R1\",\"requirement\":\"node1 (VyOS) configured as DNS resolver answering inventory.internal with node2's address on the shared 10.100.232.0/24 network\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS static-host-mapping for inventory.internal -> 10.100.232.11 was applied and committed/saved; dig from node1 and from clients confirms resolution. Config was applied via manual validation (cmd-17d7c20f5f8c469b/cmd-80215e19446840bc) and then confirmed reproducible/applied through the Ansible playbook (cmd-13bbd69976c54166). Configuration persisted and worked identically after a full node1 reboot (cmd-44bcf48e207440e4).\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-17d7c20f5f8c469b\",\"cmd-80215e19446840bc\",\"cmd-13bbd69976c54166\",\"cmd-44bcf48e207440e4\"]},{\"id\":\"R2\",\"requirement\":\"node1 forwards all other DNS queries upstream\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"VyOS 'service dns forwarding' with name-server 10.100.232.1 configured; dig for example.com against node1 resolves correctly both before and after the node1 restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-80215e19446840bc\",\"cmd-44bcf48e207440e4\"]},{\"id\":\"R3\",\"requirement\":\"node2 and node3 configured to resolve through node1\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"resolvconf head override pointing at 10.100.232.10 installed via the Ansible playbook on both clients; getent hosts confirms inventory.internal and a public name resolve through node1 both immediately after the playbook run and after independent restarts of node2 and node3.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-13bbd69976c54166\",\"cmd-4008b74dea8346b6\",\"cmd-f501256393354695\",\"cmd-912bce5e3e2b42fd\"]},{\"id\":\"R4\",\"requirement\":\"Implementation performed using Ansible from the control node\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"An inventory/ansible.cfg/playbook.yml were created on node4 (the designated control node) and ansible-playbook was run against node1/node2/node3, with a subsequent idempotent re-run also completing successfully.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-afa17fff762f41d6\",\"cmd-13bbd69976c54166\",\"cmd-4008b74dea8346b6\"]},{\"id\":\"R5\",\"requirement\":\"Provider-wide node-restart evidence protocol executed on every managed node (node1-node4) with pre-restart baseline, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service/data/cluster state\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"For each of node1, node2, node3, and node4, distinct baseline boot_id, a reboot command, a subsequent different boot_id, and post-reboot verification of DNS/resolver functionality (and, for node4, a full successful playbook re-run) are all directly observed in the evidence, matching the fixed lifecycle boot-identity cross-check.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-1a5e49c03bad42c0\",\"cmd-b1b6125519ca48e8\",\"cmd-1674728b796c40df\",\"cmd-44bcf48e207440e4\",\"cmd-6f4979fbeb814b84\",\"cmd-9ccfd46a8b7142f6\",\"cmd-368ebe4ed1d04131\",\"cmd-f501256393354695\",\"cmd-202eacd1315e4398\",\"cmd-920b37a68b7244a6\",\"cmd-a1ded998e60e4694\",\"cmd-912bce5e3e2b42fd\",\"cmd-d60ef54c87cb476c\",\"cmd-065ae67192f7430c\",\"cmd-24a15977601441b5\",\"cmd-1d3caeaade2b4cbd\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.85,\"summary\":\"The bulk of state-changing commands were clearly tied to necessary prerequisites (SSH key setup for Ansible connectivity to node1/node2/node3) or to applying and verifying the DNS configuration itself. One unnecessary, bounded mutation occurred: the executor wrote /root/.ssh/authorized_keys on node1 (cmd-7bf2d980a3434a23) in an attempt to enable root SSH login, which was refused by sshd (ROOT LOGIN REFUSED, observed in cmd-dda4a11b91eb4aeb) and was then fully reverted (cmd-ef76c8fd24c6474e removed the file) once the executor switched to the working 'vyos' user. Several ansible-playbook and raw-SSH command attempts failed during iterative debugging of quoting/escaping issues (e.g. cmd-69a29de7df044361, cmd-3daa64e0816c40e1, cmd-8db6df840f794991, cmd-5ce7590ffb284467, cmd-8bcdb165f6364a05) but these were re-attempts of the same intended configuration, not divergent or destructive mutations, and did not leave residue. The lifecycle diff between after-prepare and after-executor shows only expected changes (new boot identities from restarts, DNS service now listening on node1, rotated systemd-private temp dirs) with no failed services, no package-health issues, and no unexplained residue.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-7bf2d980a3434a23\",\"cmd-dda4a11b91eb4aeb\",\"cmd-ef76c8fd24c6474e\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"The executor successfully implemented node1 as a VyOS DNS forwarder answering inventory.internal with node2's address and forwarding all other queries upstream, and configured node2/node3 to resolve through node1, all via an Ansible playbook run from the designated control node (node4). Functional verification (dig/getent) confirms correct resolution both immediately after configuration and after each node's individual restart, with idempotent playbook re-runs also succeeding. The mandatory provider-wide restart-evidence protocol was completed for all four managed nodes with clear baseline, restart, changed-boot-identity, and recovery evidence, including a full playbook re-run from node4 after its own reboot.\",\"limitations\":[\"The first successful Ansible-driven application of node1's DNS config (cmd-13bbd69976c54166) occurred after the same configuration had already been applied manually via raw SSH; because the VyOS task uses ansible.builtin.raw (which reports changed by default), it cannot be fully distinguished from evidence alone whether the playbook task itself would independently apply the config from a clean state versus reporting changed due to raw-module semantics on an already-configured system.\",\"Systemd 'listening-sockets' hygiene evidence is only available for node1 and node4; node2/node3 listening-socket observations were empty/unavailable both before and after, limiting cross-checking of unexpected service exposure on the Ubuntu clients.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"node1 (VyOS) configured as DNS resolver answering inventory.internal with node2's address on the shared 10.100.232.0/24 network","status":"satisfied","summary":"VyOS static-host-mapping for inventory.internal -> 10.100.232.11 was applied and committed/saved; dig f